:====
# A task terminated while it is suspended is answered that it is cancelled. One that ignores the
# answer runs on, and the termination ends it later, at a wait or a poll; its cleanup runs.

/time/duration

do new
    . answer = false
    do finally
        . failure = Task().failure
        if failure
            -- "cleanup saw $failure.message"
        -- "suspend answered $answer"
    answer = Task().suspend()
    Semaphore().wait()
    -- "unexpected resume"

50ms.wait()
